  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EVALUATION OF THE REPRODUCTIVE BIOLOGY OF THE KEMPS RIDLEY SEA TURTLE AT RANCHO NUEVO, MEXICO: IMPLICATONS FOR CONSERVATION AND ECOLOGY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recipient will 1. evaluate clutch frequency of nestng females; 2. assess hatchling sex ratios in situ and in hatcheries; 3. using DJI Inspire 1 document courtship and mating behavior, distribuution and abundance of KR in near-shore waters before and during the nesting season; 4. determine emergence times of corral versus in situ nests; and 5. evaluate pivotal temperature under natural incubation regimes.</narrative>
  </description>
